 ## Background
-The Level-0 Mask Classifier is part of the NeuralVDB framework, which proposes replacing the lowest two levels of the VDB tree structure with neural networks. This approach creates a hierarchical neural representation where the root and upper internal levels remain unchanged [S1]. The method was introduced in the paper "NeuralVDB: High-resolution Sparse Volume Representation using Hierarchical Neural Networks" [S1].
